From c6378e680291a5f3e215fc8afad99ff1887480c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:12:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add getGpsDebugData

Surfaces the GNSS engine's own diagnostics over LS2: its position and time
estimates and what it believes about each satellite. That is the question worth
asking when a device streams NMEA at 1Hz but never reports a satellite in view,
and until now there was no way to ask it from outside the HAL.

The data comes from nyx_gps_get_debug_data, which the hybris GPS module answers
from IGnssDebug. That extension is optional, so a HAL without it is reported as
LOCATION_GPS_NYX_SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE - "Location data source not present" -
rather than as a failed call, because the call did not fail; the device simply
has nothing to say.

The payload is text rather than structured fields on purpose: the HAL's
DebugData carries a variable-length satellite array whose element layout is not
pinned down across HAL versions, so neither nyx nor this service models it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]
